WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.778
<v Narrator>A grain co-op's bid line is usually a recording,

2
00:00:05.858 --> 00:00:08.920
<v Narrator>made once in the morning, while prices move all day.

3
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:13.498
<v Narrator>Growers press through a menu for a number that may already be stale.

4
00:00:13.578 --> 00:00:15.350
<v Narrator>This agent just answers.

5
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.960
<v Narrator>Growers call a Teams phone number, through Teams Phone extensibility.

6
00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:31.197
<v Narrator>Azure Communication Services Call Automation bridges the audio to Voice Live,

7
00:00:31.277 --> 00:00:34.140
<v Narrator>where GPT Realtime holds the conversation.

8
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.726
<v Narrator>Your server prices every quote.

9
00:00:36.806 --> 00:00:41.010
<v Narrator>To sell or lock a price, the merchandiser takes the call in Teams.

10
00:00:43.411 --> 00:00:46.808
<v Narrator>Dale Meyer sells grain at the co-op's Riverside elevator.

11
00:00:46.888 --> 00:00:48.921
<v Narrator>He calls for today's corn bid.

12
00:00:49.886 --> 00:00:51.754
<v Agent>Contoso Grain Co-op bid line.

13
00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:53.596
<v Agent>I'm an automated assistant.

14
00:00:53.676 --> 00:00:56.228
<v Agent>Bids are subject to change without notice.

15
00:00:56.308 --> 00:00:59.018
<v Agent>Confirm with the merchandiser before selling.

16
00:00:59.098 --> 00:01:01.046
<v Agent>Which commodity and location?

17
00:01:02.373 --> 00:01:04.673
<v Dale>What's corn paying at Riverside?

18
00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:08.846
<v Agent>Corn at Riverside for November delivery is $4.12,

19
00:01:08.926 --> 00:01:13.888
<v Agent>that's 35 under December futures, as of 10:42 AM. Anything else?

20
00:01:15.239 --> 00:01:19.519
<v Narrator>Every word of that quote was written by your server. The agent only read it.

21
00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.580
<v Dale>And beans?

22
00:01:21.882 --> 00:01:26.273
<v Agent>Soybeans at Riverside for November delivery are $10.11,

23
00:01:26.353 --> 00:01:31.462
<v Agent>that's 18 under November futures, as of 10:41 AM. Anything else?

24
00:01:32.804 --> 00:01:34.754
<v Dale>That's all, thanks.

25
00:01:35.057 --> 00:01:38.227
<v Agent>Thanks for calling Contoso Grain Co-op. Goodbye.

26
00:01:39.596 --> 00:01:43.178
<v Narrator>The model never sees a raw bid, basis or futures price,

27
00:01:43.258 --> 00:01:46.106
<v Narrator>so it has no number of its own to invent.

28
00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:51.079
<v Narrator>Prices age, and a stale price is a wrong one.

29
00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:55.220
<v Narrator>Your server decides whether a quote may still be called current.

30
00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:57.620
<v Caller>Soybeans at Riverside?

31
00:01:57.939 --> 00:02:02.330
<v Agent>Soybeans at Riverside for November delivery are $10.11,

32
00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:07.519
<v Agent>that's 18 under November futures, as of 10:41 AM. Anything else?

33
00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:13.626
<v Narrator>At 10:45, those futures are four minutes old, inside the twenty-minute window.

34
00:02:13.706 --> 00:02:15.340
<v Narrator>So the quote is live.

35
00:02:16.095 --> 00:02:19.875
<v Narrator>The clock jumps to 11:20, and the caller asks again.

36
00:02:22.264 --> 00:02:23.304
<v Caller>Say that again?

37
00:02:23.627 --> 00:02:27.187
<v Agent>Soybeans at Riverside for November delivery are $10.11,

38
00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:30.480
<v Agent>that's 18 under November futures, as of 10:41 AM.

39
00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.507
<v Agent>These prices may be delayed. Anything else?

40
00:02:34.875 --> 00:02:36.535
<v Narrator>A repeat is never a replay.

41
00:02:36.615 --> 00:02:38.175
<v Narrator>The server checked again,

42
00:02:38.255 --> 00:02:41.585
<v Narrator>found thirty-nine-minute-old futures, and added the caveat.

43
00:02:42.337 --> 00:02:45.817
<v Narrator>Now it's two in the afternoon, after the 1:20 close.

44
00:02:48.219 --> 00:02:50.779
<v Caller>Repeat that, please.

45
00:02:51.082 --> 00:02:56.422
<v Agent>As of the last close, soybeans at Riverside for November delivery were $10.05,

46
00:02:56.502 --> 00:03:00.032
<v Agent>that's 18 under November futures. Anything else?

47
00:03:01.394 --> 00:03:05.964
<v Narrator>No live price exists now, so the agent gives the last settlement, and says so.

48
00:03:08.346 --> 00:03:14.246
<v Narrator>Three answers to one question, each decided by policy code. The trail shows why.

49
00:03:16.302 --> 00:03:19.358
<v Narrator>Dale calls back. Reading a bid is the agent's job.

50
00:03:19.438 --> 00:03:23.222
<v Narrator>Advising on it, or locking it in, belongs to the merchandiser.

51
00:03:24.223 --> 00:03:26.293
<v Dale>Corn at Riverside for December?

52
00:03:26.607 --> 00:03:30.517
<v Agent>Corn at Riverside for December delivery is $4.14,

53
00:03:30.597 --> 00:03:35.637
<v Agent>that's 33 under December futures, as of 10:42 AM. Anything else?

54
00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:39.760
<v Dale>Should I lock that in now, or wait?

55
00:03:40.051 --> 00:03:43.711
<v Agent>I can't advise on that, but the merchandiser can talk it through with you.

56
00:03:45.076 --> 00:03:50.286
<v Narrator>No tool on this line can lock, book or contract a price. Watch the Teams panel.

57
00:03:51.109 --> 00:03:55.119
<v Dale>Okay, lock in 5,000 bushels at that price.

58
00:03:55.462 --> 00:03:59.738
<v Agent>I can't lock in or book a price on this line — only a merchandiser can.

59
00:03:59.818 --> 00:04:03.072
<v Agent>Connecting you with the Riverside merchandiser now.

60
00:04:04.426 --> 00:04:05.636
<v Narrator>Nothing was locked.

61
00:04:05.716 --> 00:04:09.409
<v Narrator>The Riverside merchandiser's Teams client rings with Dale's last quote,

62
00:04:09.489 --> 00:04:11.256
<v Narrator>his own words and the reason.

63
00:04:13.683 --> 00:04:15.823
<v Narrator>The model held the conversation.

64
00:04:15.903 --> 00:04:20.733
<v Narrator>Your server decided every quote, caveat, refusal and handoff, and counted them.

65
00:04:22.377 --> 00:04:24.800
<v Narrator>Under the hood, the model only converses.

66
00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:29.017
<v Narrator>It passes on what the grower asked, and reads back the server's sentence.

67
00:04:29.467 --> 00:04:33.385
<v Narrator>The server decides the rest: the location, whether a price is live,

68
00:04:33.465 --> 00:04:37.357
<v Narrator>delayed or missing, and that every lock request goes to a person.

69
00:04:39.557 --> 00:04:43.510
<v Narrator>Making it yours is mostly configuration: your elevators, merchandisers

70
00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:47.157
<v Narrator>and hours, your bid sheet, market hours and freshness window.

71
00:04:47.607 --> 00:04:50.781
<v Narrator>A licensed feed replaces one fixture class, and the spec

72
00:04:50.861 --> 00:04:54.217
<v Narrator>and tests give your coding agent the rules that must hold.

73
00:04:56.817 --> 00:04:58.300
<v Narrator>Bid and price lookup.

74
00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:03.017
<v Narrator>Run it in simulation in two minutes, then connect it to your own Teams number.
